2TfWrZR","sux8kYHe","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3dmwKy5/76dd9e7bc737a02b723730ab34f536ab43936980.png","https://github.com/Glitchfiend/GlitchCore/issues","https://github.com/Glitchfiend/GlitchCore","https://discord.gg/GyyzU6T",[31800],{"id":3122,"platform":30578,"url":31801},"https://www.paypal.com/donate/?business=AdubbzG@gmail.com&item_name=GlitchCore+(from+modrinth.com)&cy_code=USD",[],13456225,"6eCO2HAn",{"client_side":29960,"server_side":29960,"game_versions":31806,"id":31807,"slug":31808,"project_type":31,"team":31809,"organization":3571,"title":31810,"description":31811,"body":31812,"body_url":3571,"published":31813,"updated":31814,"approved":31815,"queued":31816,"status":29947,"requested_status":29947,"moderator_message":3571,"license":31817,"downloads":31818,"followers":30221,"categories":31819,"additional_categories":31820,"loaders":31821,"versions":31822,"icon_url":31824,"issues_url":3571,"source_url":3571,"wiki_url":3571,"discord_url":3571,"donation_urls":31825,"gallery":31826,"color":31827,"thread_id":31828,"monetization_status":30006},[820],"s2brX0Ux","tomc-creefern","VhWFUGBJ","TOMC - CreeFern","Why would a creature self-destruct as a means of attack? To reproduce!","![Creefern, or the Creeper Fern](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/b8166a499dcd0a3c77b1123597de36e2cf0c6109.png)\n# OVERVIEW\n**Why would a creature abandon its survival instinct and instead resort to self-explosion as a means of attack on its evolutionary journey -- For the sake of reproduction!**\n\nThis MOD belongs to my TOMC (Tales of Minecraft) series. If you like it, please continue to follow us! My partners and I will continue to produce contents like this as much as possible!\n\n# FEATURES\nAfter installing this mod, a new plant called \"Creefern\", which means Creeper-Fern, will be naturally generated in the overworld, and will be generated more in jungle biomes. It has 3 growth stages and can be ripened with bone meal. When fully ripened, it will turn into a Creeper entity. Most importantly, a creeper's explosion will spread a large number of creeferns within a certain range, so remember to clean them up in time! What's more, The Creeper Spores dropped by the first 2 stages of creeferns can be used for composting, while the 3rd stage of creeferns that have not yet transformed into a creeper entity will directly drop several Gunpowder!\n\n# STATEMENT\n**Feel free to add it to your modpack if you want!**\n\nThis mod can be approximated as a high-version remake of the \"_Organic Creepers_\" mod by Konlii, which has been discontinued. Actually my mod has a considerable amount of my personal understanding and modification compared to Konlii, and I have no direct relationship with Konlii.\n\n\n\nPERSONAL HOMEPAGE: https://space.bilibili.com/583103610","2025-01-17T02:33:20.673481Z","2025-01-17T02:40:32.806474Z","2025-01-18T06:56:59.402738Z","2025-01-17T02:42:16.627378Z",{"id":30702,"name":30703,"url":3571},112,[30,191,316],[],[385],[31823],"8z8UKAYf","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s2brX0Ux/7422b9858bbee2ab22b68b086532dd3a9d80fc89_96.webp",[],[],2313496,"UFsbLYEM",{"client_side":30008,"server_side":29960,"game_versions":31830,"id":31831,"slug":31832,"project_type":31,"team":31833,"organization":3571,"title":31834,"description":31835,"body":31836,"body_url":3571,"published":31837,"updated":31838,"approved":31839,"queued":31840,"status":29947,"requested_status":29947,"moderator_message":3571,"license":31841,"downloads":30982,"followers":30221,"categories":31842,"additional_categories":31843,"loaders":31844,"versions":31845,"icon_url":31847,"issues_url":3571,"source_url":31848,"wiki_url":3571,"discord_url":3571,"donation_urls":31849,"gallery":31850,"color":31851,"thread_id":31852,"monetization_status":30006},[941,869,863,826,820,772,769,739],"s2xFz48W","feathertp","PzI8PDPY","FeatherTP","A super lightweight Random TP plugin that follows the philosophy of \"Do one thing, and do it well\"","# FeatherTP (Feather Teleport)\n\nFeatherTP is a Minecraft plugin that allows players to randomly teleport to safe locations within the Minecraft world. This plugin is lightweight and easy to use, making it ideal for servers that want to add random teleportation features without impacting server performance.\n\n## Features\n\n- Random teleportation to safe locations\n- Configurable teleportation range and center position\n- Cooldown settings between teleportations\n- Support for multiple worlds (world_nether, world_the_end, etc.)\n- Reload command to reload the configuration\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Download the `.jar` file from [Releases](https://github.com/Lightnabz/FeatherTP/releases).\n2. Place the `.jar` file into the `plugins` folder on your Minecraft server.\n3. Restart your Minecraft server.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use FeatherTP, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Random Teleport Command**  \n    Players can use the `/rtp` command to randomly teleport to a safe location. Additionally, the plugin supports aliases such as `/tpr` and `/ltp`.  \n    Example:  \n    ```\n    /rtp\n    /tpr\n    /ltp\n    ```\n\n2. **Admin Commands**  \n    - Reload the plugin configuration:  \n      ```\n      /feathertp reload\n      ```\n      This command reloads the `config.yml` file without restarting the server.\n\n3. **Permissions**  \n    - `feathertp.use`: Allows players to use the `/rtp`, `/tpr`, and `/ltp` commands.  \n    - `feathertp.admin`: Grants access to admin commands like `/feathertp reload`.\n\nMake sure to configure permissions in your server's permission management plugin (e.g., LuckPerms) to control access to these commands.\n\n## Configuration\n\nThis plugin uses a `config.yml` file for configuration. Below is an example configuration structure:\n\n```yaml\npermissions:\n    require-use-permission: true  # If true, only players with the `feathertp.use` permission can use /rtp\n\nworld:\n    teleport:\n        random:\n            minRange: 100        # Minimum range for teleportation\n            maxRange: 1000       # Maximum range for teleportation\n            centerX: 0           # X-coordinate of the teleportation center\n            centerZ: 0           # Z-coordinate of the teleportation center\n            maxTries: 10         # Number of attempts to find a safe location\n            cooldownSeconds: 30  # Cooldown in seconds between teleportations\n```\n## Building/Compiling\n\nTo build the FeatherTP plugin from source, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Clone the Repository**  \n    Clone the FeatherTP repository to your local machine:\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/Lightnabz/FeatherTP.git\n    cd FeatherTP\n    ```\n\n2. **Ensure Prerequisites**  \n    Make sure you have the following installed:\n    - [Java Development Kit (JDK)](https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase-downloads.html) (version 21 or higher)\n    - [Maven](https://maven.apache.org/)\n\n3. **Build the Plugin**  \n    Use Maven to compile the plugin and package it into a `.jar` file:\n    ```bash\n    mvn clean package\n    ```\n\n4. **Locate the Output**  \n    After the build process completes, the `.jar` file will be located in the `target` directory.\n\nYou can now use the generated `.jar` file as described in the [Installation](#installation) section.","2025-04-25T07:42:05.629896Z","2025-04-25T14:52:49.119320Z","2025-04-27T00:28:44.138409Z","2025-04-25T15:11:13.416278Z",{"id":29973,"name":29974,"url":3571},[134,303],[],[329,401,405],[31846],"Zfpq5ZQL","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s2xFz48W/94774898e56af88b35e452e8b6804cca1a076e90.png","https://github.com/LightNabz/FeatherTP/tree/main",[],[],13947861,"bXHPHHqt",{"client_side":29960,"server_side":30008,"game_versions":31854,"id":31855,"slug":31856,"project_type":12,"team":31857,"organization":3571,"title":31858,"description":31859,"body":31860,"body_url":3571,"published":31861,"updated":31862,"approved":31863,"queued":31864,"status":29947,"requested_status":29947,"moderator_message":3571,"license":31865,"downloads":31866,"followers":29976,"categories":31867,"additional_categories":31868,"loaders":31869,"versions":31870,"icon_url":31873,"issues_url":3571,"source_url":3571,"wiki_url":3571,"discord_url":3571,"donation_urls":31874,"gallery":31875,"color":31888,"thread_id":31889,"monetization_status":30006},[826,820,772,769,739,691],"s3nx29by","end-moon","Xv7rG4zr","End Moon","This texture pack changes the texture of the moon, creating the impression that it consists of endstone.","Have you ever associated Ender world with the moon? There are many mods and datapacks on the subject of this association. This texture pack can be an addition to all this. The moon will now be textured as if it \nconsists of multiple endstone blocks. This moon, just like vanilla moon, has variations in appearance.","2025-04-24T01:32:12.330663Z","2025-04-28T13:45:43.163581Z","2025-04-27T05:29:33.899112Z","2025-04-24T07:46:01.460632Z",{"id":30021,"name":10,"url":3571},217,[15,100,139],[57,197,245,268,307],[377],[31871,31872],"GJVNt0dI","8obawgYK","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/77433c08c8dc04eb346823f1debe490aea2dee31.png",[],[31876,31880,31884],{"url":31877,"raw_url":31878,"featured":439,"title":3571,"description":3571,"created":31879,"ordering":29995},"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/1b478602ad9daebf4692c994ee476fb89f131cb1_350.webp","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/1b478602ad9daebf4692c994ee476fb89f131cb1.png","2025-04-28T13:43:33.194794Z",{"url":31881,"raw_url":31882,"featured":439,"title":3571,"description":3571,"created":31883,"ordering":29995},"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/67edd757677cd4ce93b395ad8442180e046087a3_350.webp","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/67edd757677cd4ce93b395ad8442180e046087a3.png","2025-04-28T13:43:25.238618Z",{"url":31885,"raw_url":31886,"featured":439,"title":3571,"description":3571,"created":31887,"ordering":29995},"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/6ebb553b6308096d0e8f6d823343d5b23efbf7fe_350.webp","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s3nx29by/images/6ebb553b6308096d0e8f6d823343d5b23efbf7fe.png","2025-04-24T01:37:15.477117Z",14805417,"Q14XBFNU",{"client_side":29960,"server_side":29960,"game_versions":31891,"id":31892,"slug":31893,"project_type":31,"team":31894,"organization":3571,"title":31895,"description":31896,"body":31897,"body_url":3571,"published":31898,"updated":31899,"approved":31900,"queued":31901,"status":29947,"requested_status":29950,"moderator_message":3571,"license":31902,"downloads":31903,"followers":30273,"categories":31904,"additional_categories":31905,"loaders":31906,"versions":31907,"icon_url":31910,"issues_url":3571,"source_url":3571,"wiki_url":3571,"discord_url":3571,"donation_urls":31911,"gallery":31914,"color":31915,"thread_id":31916,"monetization_status":30006},[1022],"s31nHiVq","pixelmon-factory","8uiEc9xg","Pixelmon Factory","Pixelmon Factory is a mod that bridges Pixelmon X Create together. This was inspired by Create: Pixelfactory.","IS THIS MOD STILL GETTING SUPPORT: Currently, yes. I will add more information about what versions later on.\n\nPixelmon Factory is an evolving mod focused on integrating the Create and Pixelmon experiences to expand crafting and automation for Pokémon items. Currently, the mod introduces a range of custom crafting recipes, fluids, and item enhancements to support a unique Pixelmon crafting workflow. As it's still in early development, the mod lacks substantial planned content, and many features are still being refined. Player feedback is appreciated to help shape future updates and expand the mod's functionality.\n\nAll assets that have been used are retextures or made by me.\n\nIf you have ANY suggestions of features you would like to see in the mod please let me know by joining the discord on this page.\n\n\n\nPermissions & Licences:\n\nCreate Wrench: From [Create](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/create) (If the owners of Create would like me to remove it, then please message me.)\n\nPokeball: From [IconDuck](https://iconduck.com/icons/315706/pokeball)\n\nMore description will be added later.","2024-10-28T17:16:44.075643Z","2024-11-09T19:50:34.915863Z","2024-11-01T02:24:41.641771Z","2024-10-28T18:01:38.260795Z",{"id":29973,"name":29974,"url":3571},2152,[134,175,279],[288],[354],[31908,31909],"61nFfnzW","mK5BrbRg","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/s31nHiVq/ea747d7a44c0f5974a55b0b1e97667a869931901_96.webp",[31912],{"id":3122,"platform":30578,"url":31913},"https://www.paypal.com/paypalme/Seristic",[],11939118,"nGl1xYXO",{"client_side":29960,"server_side":29960,"game_versions":31918,"id":31919,"slug":31920,"project_type":31,"team":31921,"organization":3571,"title":31922,"description":31923,"body":31924,"body_url":3571,"published":31925,"updated":31926,"approved":31925,"queued":3571,"status":29947,"requested_status":3571,"moderator_message":3571,"license":31927,"downloads":31930,"followers":31931,"categories":31932,"additional_categories":31933,"loaders":31934,"versions":31935,"icon_url":31944,"issues_url":3571,"source_url":3571,"wiki_url":3571,"discord_url":3571,"donation_urls":31945,"gallery":31946,"color":31960,"thread_id":31919,"monetization_status":30006},[1250],"s2WrV3mN","cozycabincore","9VJlOhjc","Cozy Cabincore - C3","Redwoods, flowers, cabin logs, and more!","This mod adds a new type of tree to the Old Growth Forests, the Redwood. Redwood and Spruce will now drop Pine Sap, which can be combined with a Bottle of Honey to make a Bottle of Sticky Pitch. Pitch is used to make Cabin Logs. Several other new decorative blocks and plants can be found and created, such as new flowers in both Old Growth Forests and Birch Forests, or planks which can be made from Bark.","2022-06-16T20:32:24.819707Z","2022-09-15T04:51:00.238877Z",{"id":31928,"name":31929,"url":3571},"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike 4.0 International",2163,14,[30,100,316],[],[346,354,409],[31936,31937,31938,31939,31940,31941,31942,31943],"1rDHBqHs","jNfPvusk","9eRKdLXr","